CHAPTER VI

DUTIES AND OBLIGATIONS OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT

Article 15

1. The Regional Government has the duty to carry out prevention, handling and recovery efforts for victims of violence against Women and Children, by:a. collecting data and information about Women and Children Victims of Violence;
b. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
c. conducting education on anti-violence values against children and women; and  d. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection for Women and Children victims of violence.
2. The Regional Government is obliged to carry out prevention, handling and recovery efforts for victims of violence against Women and Children, provide and organize services for victims in the form of:a. providing and facilitating the establishment of integrated services for victims by involving institutions and community elements;
b. encouraging public awareness about the importance of protection for victims; and  c. empowering communities to prevent acts of violence.

CHAPTER VIII

PREVENTION OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 17

1. The Government in efforts to prevent acts of violence against women and children carries out empowerment of families, parents, communities by providing information, guidance and or counseling.
2. In addition to empowerment and support as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government carries out efforts as follows:a. increasing the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
c. endeavoring to create employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and concern for prevention and from acts of violence against women and children;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and or care about women and children victims of violence.

Article 18

1. Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in article 16, is carried out by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field ofa. social;
b. health;
c. education;
d. employment;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental;
g. security and order;
2. Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out in an integrated and continuous manner based on existing regulations.

Article 3

Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence aims to provide protection and services that include aspects of prevention, service and assistance, reunification and empowerment.

Article 4 The implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence aims to:
a. prevent all forms of acts of violence including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation of women and children;
c. protect and provide a sense of security for victims of acts of violence;
d. provide services to victims of violence and;
e. carry out comprehensive recovery for victims.

CHAPTER VII

INSTITUTIONS PROVIDING PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS

Article 16

1. The Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center (PPT) as the Organizing, Prevention and Protection Institution for Women and Children Victims of Violence in the region.
